//! §41 layout fixtures OBSERVED ON MAINNET. **GENERATED — do not hand-edit.**
//!
//! Generated by `tools/gen_layout_fixtures.py` from a live Helius RPC probe of
//! the pump.fun program `6EF8rrecthR5Dkzon8Nwu78hRvfCKubJ14M5uBEwF6P`.
//!
//! Sample: **400 transactions**, 547 pump.fun instructions,
//! 259 identified. Every row below carries the **real** verifying
//! signature and slot of a transaction that exhibited that account count, so
//! `LayoutRegistry::record_verified` accepts it on its merits — no placeholder
//! passes the guard, and none is fabricated here.
//!
//! ## What the chain actually shows
//!
//! | instruction | accounts | notes |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `buy` | **18** | both token programs; cashback does not change the count |
//! | `buy_exact_sol_in` | **18** | same layout as `buy` |
//! | `sell` | **16** | no cashback (+bonding_curve_v2 +BuybackVault) |
//! | `sell` | **17** | cashback (+user_volume_accumulator) |
//! | `buy_v2` | 27 | **not built by this engine** |
//! | `sell_v2` | 26 / 27 | **not built by this engine** |
//!
//! The old hand-rolled block registered **17** for a buy. No mainnet buy with 17
//! accounts exists in this sample: 17 is what `FeeTail::None` produces, and per
//! Rev-18 a 17-account buy fails on chain (`Custom(6062)`,
//! BuybackFeeRecipientMissing). Registering it was what let the gate accept a
//! layout the chain rejects. It is **not** registered here.
//!
//! `non_sol_quote` is false for every row: pump.fun bonding curves are
//! SOL-quoted, and the builder derives this dimension as
//! `quote_mint != WSOL_MINT`. (`docs/fixtures/layouts.json` records
//! `non_sol_quote: true` for pumpfun rows — that field does not agree with the
//! builder and is **not** trusted here; see the plan doc.)
//!
//! ## Coverage gaps (deliberate, fail-closed)
//!
//! `buy_v2`/`sell_v2` are **not** registered, because this engine never builds
//! them — registering a count the builder cannot emit would only widen the gate.
//! If pump.fun retires the legacy `buy` path, the builder must learn `buy_v2`
//! before those trades work; the gate will refuse rather than mis-build.

